From 6981e6b332dedc7359e6e573c82e779efa8daf31 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?=E9=AB=98=E5=BA=86=E4=B8=B0?= <gao.qingfeng@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 23:14:50 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 07/29] perf(chunk/cache): drop forced run_pending_tasks from
 insert_hot hot path

Closes #11 (gqf2008/brewfs)

insert_hot awaited hot_cache.run_pending_tasks() after every insert,
synchronously draining all pending moka maintenance on the hot read
backfill path.

Evaluation (criterion, benches/brewfs_bench.rs::bench_insert_hot, small
hot tier with eviction churn):
- before: 3.04 us/op
- after:  2.11 us/op  (-30.2%, +43.3% throughput, p < 0.05)

Correctness: moka future Cache has no background task, but maintenance
runs automatically on get/insert once the op channel reaches a flush
point or more_entries_to_evict is set, so eviction listeners (and thus
hot_bytes) are eventually delivered with bounded lag and no permanent
leak. insert_hot's manual hot_bytes increment remains; get() sees
pending inserts (verified by the existing read-after-insert tests).

- Added bench_insert_hot A/B harness.
- Budget test now drains maintenance before asserting weighted_size()
  (weighted_size is approximate until maintenance runs).
